    "justification": "Apple-like history holds at most 12 heart-rate samples per hour (one per 5-minute slot), so the frozen gate of 30 native samples rejects every thinned hour. The frozen protocol admits an hour when at least half of its minutes hold a sample (coverage >= 0.5); under 5-minute thinning, 30 covered minutes always span at least 6 slots, so >= 6 of 12 slots (coverage >= 0.5 of slots) is the same rule at the thinned cadence. The pre-scoring audit confirms it: all 46,406 hours the frozen protocol admits keep >= 6 thinned samples (min 6, p01 8, median 12), and the gate newly admits 268 hours (0.6%). Coverage stays >= 0.5; target gates stay on full-density labels."
